Use Boyer–Moore voting, then verify the candidate occurs strictly more than half the time. Empty input or no majority returns null. Time: O(n); auxiliary space: O(1).

```javascript
function solve(nums) {
  let candidate = null;
  let balance = 0;

  for (const value of nums) {
    if (balance === 0) {
      candidate = value;
    }
    balance += value === candidate ? 1 : -1;
  }

  let count = 0;
  for (const value of nums) {
    if (value === candidate) {
      count++;
    }
  }

  return count > nums.length / 2 ? candidate : null;
}
```

Call solve(nums) with an integer array; the input is unchanged.

