Find the rightmost ascending pair, swap its first value with the smallest greater suffix value, then reverse the suffix. If no pair exists, reverse the whole array to wrap to ascending order.

```javascript
function solve(nums) {
  let i = nums.length - 2;
  while (i >= 0 && nums[i] >= nums[i + 1]) {
    i--;
  }

  if (i >= 0) {
    let j = nums.length - 1;
    while (nums[j] <= nums[i]) {
      j--;
    }
    [nums[i], nums[j]] = [nums[j], nums[i]];
  }

  let left = i + 1;
  let right = nums.length - 1;
  while (left < right) {
    [nums[left], nums[right]] = [nums[right], nums[left]];
    left++;
    right--;
  }

  return nums;
}
```

Call solve(nums) directly; it modifies and returns the input array. Empty and singleton arrays remain unchanged, and duplicates are handled. Time: O(n); auxiliary space: O(1). No imports, exports, or stdin/stdout.

