Use a monotonic stack of unresolved indices. Equal temperatures remain unresolved because only strictly warmer days count. Time: O(n); space: O(n).

```javascript
function solve(temperatures) {
  const result = new Array(temperatures.length).fill(0);
  const stack = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < temperatures.length; i++) {
    while (
      stack.length > 0 &&
      temperatures[i] > temperatures[stack[stack.length - 1]]
    ) {
      const day = stack.pop();
      result[day] = i - day;
    }
    stack.push(i);
  }

  return result;
}
```

Call solve(temperatures) directly with the temperature array; it returns the result array.

