- solve("", "a") → []: p is longer than s, so it returns immediately.
- solve("ab", "abc") → []: the same early return prevents any partial-window match.
- solve("abab", "ab") → [0, 1, 2]: initially the differences are {a:-1, b:-1}. Adding a leaves {b:-1}; adding b clears the map and records 0. Next, adding a and removing the outgoing a clears it again, recording 1. Adding b and removing the outgoing b records 2. This tests overlapping matches and identical incoming/outgoing characters—the most likely sliding-window failure.
- solve("ac", "ab") → []: the full window leaves {b:-1, c:1}, so it is rejected.

