Consume values largest-first, including subtractive pairs, to produce the canonical Roman numeral.

```javascript
function solve(n) {
  const entries = [
    [1000, 'M'], [900, 'CM'], [500, 'D'], [400, 'CD'],
    [100, 'C'], [90, 'XC'], [50, 'L'], [40, 'XL'],
    [10, 'X'], [9, 'IX'], [5, 'V'], [4, 'IV'], [1, 'I']
  ];
  let result = '';

  for (const [value, symbol] of entries) {
    while (n >= value) {
      result += symbol;
      n -= value;
    }
  }

  return result;
}
```

Call solve(n) directly with an integer from 1 through 3999. Time and space are O(1) under this fixed range: the output has at most 15 characters.

