```js
export function solve(ops) {
  const m = new Map();
  const out = [];

  for (const [t, op, k, v, ttl] of ops) {
    if (op === "put") {
      m.set(k, { v, end: t + ttl });
    } else {
      const x = m.get(k);
      out.push(!x || t >= x.end ? null : x.v);
    }
  }

  return out;
}
```

The restored invariant is that a stored value is returned only while `t < putTime + ttl`; at or after expiration, the lookup returns `null`. The fix changes `t > x.end` to `t >= x.end`, preserving the synchronous API and requiring no dependencies or test edits.

