• solve("", ""): n is zero, so the early return gives 0.
• solve("", "abc"): the strings swap, giving m=3 and n=0; the early return gives 3.
• solve("a", "a"): dp starts as [0,1]. Resetting dp[0] gives [1,1]; the matching diagonal costs 0, producing [1,0] and returning 0.
