```javascript
function solve(weights, values, capacity) {
  const dp = new Array(capacity + 1).fill(0);

  for (let i = 0; i < weights.length; i++) {
    for (let c = capacity; c >= weights[i]; c--) {
      dp[c] = Math.max(dp[c], dp[c - weights[i]] + values[i]);
    }
  }

  return dp[capacity];
}
```

Call directly with matching weight/value arrays, positive integer weights, nonnegative values, and a nonnegative integer capacity. Descending capacity updates ensure each item is used at most once; empty inputs or zero capacity return 0. Time: O(n × capacity); auxiliary space: O(capacity).

